@@ header docstring
  * Usage:
  *   node scripts/promote-shopvox-to-native.mjs --customer=<shopvox_customer_uuid> [--dry-run] [--apply]
+ *   node scripts/promote-shopvox-to-native.mjs --customers=<file> [--dry-run] [--apply] [--verbose] [--progress=<file>]
  *
  * --dry-run is the default. --apply is required to actually write anything.
  * Passing both, or neither with --apply, is not possible — --apply must be
  * explicit and alone overrides the default.
+ * --customer and --customers are mutually exclusive; exactly one is required.
+ *
+ * WIDE-RUN HARDENING (added 2026-08-25, for the ~4,500-customer run — not
+ * yet exercised against anything, built-only per instruction):
+ *
+ * - RETRY: every Supabase read and write goes through withRetry()
+ *   (scripts/lib/retry.mjs — fetchAllRows() carries its own copy). Retries
+ *   with exponential backoff (5 attempts, ~15.5s max) on a thrown network
+ *   failure, HTTP 429, or HTTP 5xx. Does NOT retry a 4xx PostgREST/Postgres
+ *   error (schema mismatch, constraint violation, bad input) — those are
+ *   real bugs and still fail immediately. Same shape as the EPERM retry fix
+ *   in shopvox-capture.mjs's flushQueue.
+ *
+ * - --customers=<file>: newline-delimited ShopVOX customer uuids (blank
+ *   lines / #-comments ignored, duplicates deduped, order preserved). Each
+ *   is promoted through the same per-customer logic --customer uses
+ *   (refactored into promoteOneCustomer()). One customer's failure is
+ *   caught, logged, tallied, and does NOT stop the run.
+ *
+ * - RESUMABILITY (--apply + --customers only): after a customer's promotion
+ *   finishes writing successfully, its shopvox uuid is appended to a
+ *   progress file (default scripts/state/promote-progress.txt, override
+ *   with --progress=<file>). A uuid already in that file is skipped on
+ *   re-run. A FAILED customer is never added, so it's retried automatically
+ *   next run. --dry-run + --customers always processes the full list and
+ *   never touches the progress file (cheap review, not "work done").
+ *
+ * - LOGGING: --customer mode is unchanged (always fully verbose). --customers
+ *   mode defaults to one summary line per customer + a final tally; pass
+ *   --verbose for the full per-table report on every customer too.
  *
 (... rest of docstring — generated-columns section etc. — unchanged ...)

